Map each network device (router, switch, hub) to the correct OSI layer and describe how 
each contributes to compliance with network segmentation requirements.

                               Answer to 1a
Routers operate at the network layer of the OSI model,making routing decisions based on 
on IP routers use IP addresses to determine the best path for data to travel between 
networks 

Switches operate at the data link layer of the OSI model and are more efficient at directing 
traffic 

Hubs operates at the physical layer of the OSI model and broadcast data to all devices on the 
network regardless of the intended recipient 


